.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH powerlinux-shortcuts 1  "PowerLinux 0.1.0" "PowerLinux Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
powerlinux\-shortcuts \- Manage GNOME keybindings for desktops without the GlobalShortcuts portal
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpowerlinux shortcuts\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage GNOME keybindings for desktops without the GlobalShortcuts portal
.PP
Adds or removes custom shortcuts in GNOME Settings (via gsettings) that run `powerlinux trigger`. Other custom shortcuts are left untouched.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBpowerlinux shortcuts install [\-\-dry\-run]\fR
Add Super+Shift+T, C and E (or your configured keys) to GNOME Settings
.RS
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR: Print the gsettings commands instead of running them
.RE
.TP
\fBpowerlinux shortcuts remove [\-\-dry\-run]\fR
Remove the keybindings added by `install`
.RS
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR: Print the gsettings commands instead of running them
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Preview the gsettings commands:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux shortcuts install \-\-dry\-run\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove the shortcuts again:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux shortcuts remove\fR
.fi
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpowerlinux\fR(1), \fBgsettings\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH AUTHOR
Alexis Rios\-Negron
